        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0666" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg532"/>

                <head>No. 381.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. McLane.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 27,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 330.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch, No. 549, of
                    February last, communicating to this Department the request of the French
                    authorities for information (in connection with the case of Lefevre Bougon
                    against Anthony J. Drexel <hi rendition="#italic">et al.</hi>) as to whether
                    letters rogatory, issued by the French courts, can be duly executed in this
                    country, and referring also to the reply of the Department, No. 303, of the 6th
                    ultimo, to your above-mentioned dispatch, I now inclose herewith for
                    communication to the French Government extracts from the New York code of civil
                    procedure, giving its provisions relative to taking the testimony of witnesses
                    in suits pending in foreign countries. From which it will be seen that the
                    courts in the State of New York have the most ample ability to reciprocate in
                    the matter in question.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d381-a1.xml" xpointer="d381-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
